{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And they brought the mishkan, etc.</b> They could not set it up. And because Moses had done no work at all on the mishkan, the Holy One, blessed be He, left its erection to him — for no man was able to set it up because of the weight of the planks, which no human has the strength to raise. Moses set it up. Moses said before the Holy One, blessed be He: How is it possible for a man to set it up? He said to him: Apply your hand to it, and it will appear as though you are raising it, and it will stand up and rise on its own. And this is what is written: ״הוּקַם הַמִּשְׁכָּן״ (Exodus 40) — it was raised on its own. Midrash of Rabbi Tanchuma."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:56:54.214290425Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}